.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/

# built output of the public launch SDK (regenerated by `npm run launch:build`)
packages/launch-sdk/dist/
packages/agent-flow/dist/

# Benchmark render artifacts. The DEVELOPMENT sheets regenerate from chain via
# `node scripts/run-art-benchmark.mjs author`, and no receipt records their digests, so
# they stay out. The run records (run.json, critiques, responses, verdicts, report.json)
# ARE committed -- they are the evidence.
#
# THE FINAL-REVIEW SHEETS ARE COMMITTED, and used not to be. Every receipt pins the
# sha256 of each holdout sheet its reviewer looked at, so ignoring them shipped
# twenty-four receipts naming evidence a checkout could not see -- `npm run
# kit:artreceipts` found this the first time it ran against a fresh copy of the tree.
# "It regenerates from chain" is a reproduction path, not a verification one: it needs an
# RPC, and it re-renders rather than reads. Round one's were committed all along, which is
# what made the asymmetry easy to miss.
artifacts/art-benchmark/*/round-*/critic-sheets/
